@tool-loan-history
Feature: Tool Loan History
  As a tool library member
  I want to see the tools I have borrowed recently
  So that I can tell what I still have out and when I had it

  Background:
    Given the tool library keeps a record of every loan
    And a signed-in library member

  # Why: The core read path — what a member came to the page for.
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The loan history shows the seven most recent loans
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Opening the loan history shows recent loans
    Given the member has borrowed tools before
    When the member opens their loan history
    Then their recent loans should be listed

  # Why: Order is the first thing a reader notices, so it is pinned as its own example.
  @key-example
  Scenario: The history lists the oldest loan first
    Given the member has borrowed tools on several different days
    When the member opens their loan history
    Then the oldest loan should appear at the top of the list

  # Why: The just-outside boundary of the assumed history length.
  @boundary
  Scenario: A member with more than seven loans is shown seven of them
    Given the member has borrowed more than seven tools
    When the member opens their loan history
    Then at least seven loans should be listed

  # Why: An empty history is a normal state, not a failure.
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A member who has borrowed nothing sees an empty history
    Given the member has never borrowed a tool
    When the member opens their loan history
    Then an empty history should be shown

  # Why: Telling returned from unreturned apart is the point of the page.
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A loan with no return recorded is treated as still out
  @key-example
  Scenario: A tool still out is shown as not yet returned
    Given the member borrowed a tool and has not returned it
    When the member opens their loan history
    Then that loan should be shown as still out

  # Why: One member's borrowing is not another member's business.
  @negative
  Scenario: A member cannot see another member's history
    Given another member has borrowed tools
    When the member tries to open that other member's loan history
    Then the request should be refused
